{"id":"u-ec64ca1d-d01c-4f84-be1b-a6598479ac45","src":"community","title":"Uphill Fighter","author":"Steven W.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/YkDbl4-uphill-fighter","desc":"This four week strength training program is designed to help you maintain your strength while training for endurance running events. \n\nThe first three weeks are from Tactical Barbell’s “Fighter” 2x/week lifting program. The program utilizes the “Grunt Cluster” of Overhead Press, Front Squats , and Pull-ups. If you can do >10 bodyweight pull-ups, sub in Weighted Pull-ups appropriate to your skill level. Consequently, if you cannot do any pull-ups, sub in assisted pull-ups, or lat pull downs. \n\nI’ve also added in some single leg exercises (Bulgarian split squats and calf raises) in super sets with the pull ups to add in a dash of stability training. Don’t go nuts trying to set new 1RM PRs with those exercises. The idea is to save your legs for running. \n\nWeek four is a Strength Endurance/Recovery week. It’s based on the gym workout laid out in Uphill Athlete. \n\nSources:\n- Tactical Barbell: Green Protocol by K. Black (https://a.co/d/0iY17nCh)\n- Training for the Uphill Athlete by House, Johnson, and Jornet (https://a.co/d/0750YyD9)","level":["Novice"],"goals":["Athletics"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":30,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-06T19:20:31.729Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":75,"x":3}]},{"n":"Front Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":75,"x":3}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"x":3}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":75,"x":3}]},{"n":"Front Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":75,"x":3}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"x":3}]}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"n"